    {
      "id": "section-10",
      "order": 10,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Rational Numbers",
      "text": "Rational numbers are numbers that can be written as a fraction of two integers, such as 1/2, -3/4, and 5. Decimals that end or repeat are also rational numbers."
    },
    {
      "id": "section-11",
      "order": 11,
      "type": "image",
      "title": "Examples of Rational Numbers",
      "imageDescription": "A visual showing fractions, whole numbers, and repeating or terminating decimals as examples of rational numbers.",
